quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  3,116,"As for the disbelievers, neither their resources nor their children will save them in the least from (the torment of) Allah. Those are the inhabitants of the Fire, and they shall remain in it forever."
  3,117,"The example of what they spend in the life of this world is like a freezing wind which strikes the harvest of a people who wronged themselves, destroying it (altogether). Allah does not wrong them, but they wrong themselves."
  3,118,"O believers! Do not take (anyone) as an intimate friend besides yourselves. They will spare no effort to ruin you. They wish you to suffer. Severe hatred is already evident from the words in their mouths, but what their hearts conceal is far worse. We have indeed made the signs clear to you if (only) you understand."
  3,119,"Here you are; you love them, but they do not love you, although you believe in all the Books. When they meet you, they say: ‘We believe,’ but when they are alone, they bite their fingertips out of rage against you. Say: ‘Die in your rage (if you wish).’ Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing of what is in the breasts."
  3,120,"If some good befalls you, it upsets them, but if some evil afflicts you, they rejoice at it. However, if you are patient and God-conscious, their scheme will not harm you in the least. Indeed, Allah comprehends whatever they are doing."
  3,121,"And (remember) when you left your family early in the morning to assign the believers their positions for the battle. And Allah is All-Hearing, All-Knowing."
